WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Support us and become VIP member 
to remove all ads from www.OpenSubtitles.org

2
00:00:12.847 --> 00:00:14.415
Hi! I'm Dick Donner.

3
00:00:14.582 --> 00:00:16.751
Or as they would like me to say.
Richard Donner.

4
00:00:16.918 --> 00:00:20.221
Of course. it's a Richard Donner film.
but--

5
00:00:20.388 --> 00:00:21.890
Dick. My friends call me Dick.

6
00:00:22.056 --> 00:00:23.824
I consider everybody out there
a friend...

7
00:00:23.991 --> 00:00:28.962
...because you people asked for and
waited to see my version of <i>Superman II</i>.

8
00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:30.731
<i>But if you hadn't asked.
and requested it...</i>

9
00:00:30.898 --> 00:00:32.933
<i>...I don't think it would've seen
the light of day.</i>

10
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.236
<i>And I thought it would lay in the vaults
of Europe and never surface again.</i>

11
00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:40.806
<i>But because of all your requests
and all your asking it came to be.</i>

12
00:00:40.973 --> 00:00:43.776
But over the past three decades...

13
00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.211
...much has happened.

14
00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:48.347
Most of all. I got gray hair
I didn't have when I started.

15
00:00:48.514 --> 00:00:50.783
But much of my film had been lost.

16
00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:55.121
And it was. as I said. in vaults and
misplaced. as films happen to be.

17
00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:56.556
And a lot of it was ruined.

18
00:00:56.722 --> 00:00:59.559
<i>But through really good research
and hard work...</i>

19
00:00:59.725 --> 00:01:01.928
<i>...every bit was found that I had shot.</i>

20
00:01:02.094 --> 00:01:06.365
But some of the film you're gonna see
in <i>Superman II</i>. I didn't shoot.

21
00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:10.536
The producers felt they wanted to
bring another director in...

22
00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:13.139
...and so he shot some of the film
you're going to see.

23
00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:17.944
<i>Nonetheless. here's </i>Superman II<i> with as
much of my work as could be salvaged.</i>

24
00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:19.378
So thanks to Warner Bros..

25
00:01:19.545 --> 00:01:22.248
thanks to all of you people
for making all this possible.

26
00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:26.184
and thank you. Michael Thau.
for reconstructing my film...

27
00:01:26.351 --> 00:01:29.955
...as close to the original version
as I intended it to be.

28
00:01:30.121 --> 00:01:33.892
I just got a kick out of seeing it.
something I never thought would happen.

29
00:01:34.059 --> 00:01:36.561
It was quite emotional; quite exciting.

30
00:01:36.728 --> 00:01:38.964
Thirty years. I hope you all enjoy it.

31
00:01:39.305 --> 00:02:39.842
